          <type>const <ref refid="classRose_1_1Location" kindref="compound">Location</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>other</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Equality and inequality.</para><para>Objects are equal if they are the same type and they point to the same location. Otherwise they are unequal.</para><para>The operator== is implemented in the base class only. For the expression <computeroutput>a == b</computeroutput> it calls both <computeroutput>a.isEqual(b)</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>b.isEqual(a)</computeroutput>, returning true only if both tests return true. Subclasses should implement <computeroutput>x.isEqual(y)</computeroutput> by dynamic casting <computeroutput>y</computeroutput> to the type of <computeroutput>x</computeroutput> and returning true if and only if the cast succeeds and <computeroutput>x</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>y</computeroutput> point to the same location.</para><para>The operator!= is implemented in the base class as the complement of operator==. </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
